  "domain": "robotics",
  "definition": "IEC 61508 is a foundational international functional safety standard published by the International Electrotechnical Commission that specifies requirements for the design, development, validation, and lifecycle management of electrical, electronic, and programmable electronic (E/E/PE) safety-related systems across all application domains. It defines Safety Integrity Levels (SIL 1\u20134) as quantitative risk-reduction targets and prescribes the development methods\u2014fault trees, FMEAs, formal methods, and software design constraints\u2014appropriate to each SIL. Sector-specific derivative standards including ISO 26262 (automotive) and EN 50128 (rail) inherit its SIL framework and lifecycle requirements.",
